From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 07:50:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wayland_vulkan: rebuild the swapchain when acquiring says
 suboptimal

Only a VK_SUBOPTIMAL_KHR from vkQueuePresentKHR made the backend build
a new swapchain; one from vkAcquireNextImageKHR went to CHECK_VK_RESULT
and the swapchain stayed. Mesa's Wayland WSI (24.0) reports a change of
the compositor's dma-buf feedback only there: when the feedback asks
for other modifiers -- a scanout tranche after the compositor failed to
put the window on a plane -- the next acquire returns
VK_SUBOPTIMAL_KHR, and the present does not.

On a QEMU virtio-gpu the cluster's swapchain images are tiled
(BROADCOM_UIF, from the host's V3D), which the guest's KMS cannot scan
out, so the compositor composed the window with the GPU every frame.
It sent a scanout tranche two seconds after start, and the swapchain
was never rebuilt.

On VK_SUBOPTIMAL_KHR from the acquire, keep the image, which can still
be presented, and set resize_pending_, so the next frame builds the
swapchain the way a resize does.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/shell/backend/wayland_vulkan/wayland_vulkan.cc
+++ b/shell/backend/wayland_vulkan/wayland_vulkan.cc
@@ -725,9 +725,18 @@
     b->InitializeSwapchain();
   }
 
-  CHECK_VK_RESULT(d.vkAcquireNextImageKHR(
+  const VkResult acquired = d.vkAcquireNextImageKHR(
       b->device_, b->swapchain_, 1'000'000'000,  // timeout (ns) 1000ms
-      nullptr, b->image_ready_fence_, &b->last_image_index_));
+      nullptr, b->image_ready_fence_, &b->last_image_index_);
+  // The image is still presentable, but the surface wants another swapchain:
+  // Mesa's Wayland WSI says so here, and only here, when the compositor's
+  // dma-buf feedback changes (a scanout tranche, for one). Make the next frame
+  // build it, as for a resize.
+  if (acquired == VK_SUBOPTIMAL_KHR) {
+    b->resize_pending_ = true;
+  } else {
+    CHECK_VK_RESULT(acquired);
+  }
 
   // Flutter Engine expects the image to be available for transitioning and
   // attaching immediately, and so we need to force a host sync here before
